"```json\n{\n  \"verdict\": \"fix_required\",\n  \"summary\": \"Most of the freeze checks out. Gold recovery (6a), recipes and E1 compile reproducibility, the legacy arm's code, the ledger hashes, the plan text copied verbatim, G3 material with no engine output, and the 81 tests are all fine. It cannot ship as is for two reasons. First, the DEV-CHECK seal has three working gaps, two of them on the path A1 is told to follow. Second, the frozen compile-rate gate already reads FAIL, so G2 can never pass whatever A1 does. Nothing has been evaluated against the ledger yet (no RUN or WAIVER entry), so all fixes can be made with `prefreeze ledger --replace-before-a1` before the anchor is published. No sealed identifier appears in this review.\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F1\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocker\",\n      \"area\": \"DEV-CHECK seal: the work directory A1 is pointed at\",\n      \"finding\": \"Freeze README lines 56-64 name the work directory and tell A1 to run `compile-frozen` and `run-physical --work W`. That directory holds DEV-CHECK material whose paths do not contain SEALED, so README rule 2 does not protect it.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Count-only check (/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-idantal/db065cf7-f766-4885-b217-ed8d7edd7ade/scratchpad/review_e4b/check_devcheck.py plus an inline count): e4b_work/gold_cases_ALL.json (written at prefreeze.py:146) has gold line coordinates for 3 DEV-CHECK cases. e4b_work/prev_pass1/freeze/cases_A1.json (the superseded V2 lists) has 5 cases from 4 families that are now sealed. prev_pass1/freeze/gold_g2a_A1.json has 1 now-sealed Gold case with its lines. g2_complete_A1, known_good_A1, repeatability_A1 and gold_transforms under prev_pass1/freeze also name sealed cases, as do 11 files in prev_pass1/legacy_control, 7 in prev_pass1/g3_truth_material, and scorecard_dryrun_noE3.json. legacy/ and compiled/dev/ contain worker outputs and compiled parts for sealed cases.\",\n      \"fix\": \"Move all DEV-CHECK and superseded material (gold_cases_ALL.json, compile_report_full.json, prev_pass1/, the sealed cases' legacy/ and compiled/ entries) to a SEALED-named location outside any directory A1 uses. Have the README tell A1 to use a fresh work directory.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F2\",\n      \"severity\": \"blocker\",\n      \"area\": \"DEV-CHECK seal: compile-frozen\",\n      \"finding\": \"`compile-frozen`, which the README tells A1 to run once, reads devcheck_SEALED.json (prefreeze.py:557 via _case_docs) and recipes_devcheck_SEALED/ (prefreeze.py:562). It then compiles all 7 DEV-CHECK recipes into A1's W/compiled/dev/. This breaks README rule 2 and amendment 4f ('A1 never sees it'). The run recorded in e4b_work/compile_frozen.log did exactly this (25 = 18 A1 + 7 sealed).\",\n      \"fix\": \"Make compile-frozen (and any other A1-facing command) default to the A1 audience: cases_A1.json and recipes/ only. Sealed recompiles happen only behind an explicit --include-sealed for the final DEV-CHECK run or R1. Add a test for this. This changes the eval fingerprint, so replace the ledger afterwards.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F3\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"area\": \"DEV-CHECK seal: gold_transforms.json, and a false leak-check claim\",\n      \"finding\": \"freeze/gold_transforms.json is A1-readable and recorded in the ledger. It carries the full rows of both DEV-CHECK Gold11 cases: case_ref, scan path and sha256, label-file path and sha256, line count, per-line lengths and the transform. Its relabel snapshot also lists those cases' relabel files and line counts. That gives A1 a direct pointer to DEV-CHECK gold files it is otherwise authorized to open. inventory.json also lists every sealed scan with sha256 and broad ids. The implementation report says 'no sealed case ref, scan sha ... in any A1-facing file'. That is false.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Count-only scan: gold_transforms.json has case_ref 7, full scan sha 11, sha12 18 and gold11_id 4 hits. inventory.json has scan sha 14, sha12 17 and broad_id 3 hits. Every other A1-facing file has 0 identifier hits; README and the two plan-threshold copies mention sealed family numbers only.\",\n      \"fix\": \"Split gold_transforms.json into an A1 part and a devcheck_SEALED part. Counts and the excluded list stay public, so 6a's 'listed before scoring' still holds and both parts are hashed. Either accept inventory.json as the documented inference-by-omission or seal its DEV-CHECK rows; the inventory_sha256 value stays recorded so the draw seed is unchanged. Correct the claim in the report and the README.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F4\",\n      \"severity\": \"major (owner/orchestrator decision needed before anchoring)\",\n      \"area\": \"Amendment 4d compile-rate gate fails by construction\",\n      \"finding\": \"physical.py:653-665 gates strict V10 and DEV on both denominators. Strict V10 over the widened 26 STEPs is 20/26 = 0.769, so G2 compile_rate = FAIL and the G2 verdict is FAIL on A1 and on DEV-CHECK whatever the engine does. The A1 dry-run scorecard confirms 'compile_rate': 'FAIL'. A1 cannot fix this: V10 lives in scripts/ (frozen under G5), and E1 changes would break the frozen compile hashes. Amendment 4d puts the 80% floor on 'the DEV_AUTO_CONFIRMED recipes: every V10/native bend'. The frozen V10\u222anative DEV recipes reach 24/26 = 0.923 (19/20 on the source tree). Strict V10 counts as 'the 4d figure' only because E1's own document labels it so.\",\n      \"fix\": \"Record an explicit decision before A1 starts. Either (a) accept that G2 is FAIL by construction in this run, or (b) gate 4d on the frozen DEV recipes and report strict V10 as a diagnostic (or keep strict V10 on the plan \u00a79 source-tree denominator, 0.80). After (b), replace the ledger. Do not change this silently after A1 starts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F5\",\n      \"severity\": \"major (sequencing)\",\n      \"area\": \"G3 truth table before any engine output\",\n      \"finding\": \"README rule 6 and amendment 7 require the visual truth table to be frozen before anyone sees engine output on those scans. All 27 A1 cases carry truth rows (203), 13 of them with section images. The README's A1 procedure still runs run-physical on every A1 list. Nothing enforces the order: load_truth_table and score_physical never compare frozen_at or the ledger entry with E3 record times.\",\n      \"fix\": \"Fill and freeze the table (2 reviewers plus a tie-break, A1 203 rows and sealed 75) and record it in the ledger before A1's first run-physical, or bar A1 from the sectioned cases until then. Optionally make the scorer reject a truth table frozen after the earliest E3 record.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F6\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"area\": \"Custody claim\",\n      \"finding\": \"README lines 86 and 143 and the report say 17139000_01.ply (BENCHMARK_V2 FRESH_SCAN_OF_CONSUMED_PART) was 'never read'. In fact the source-tree inventory hashed it (inventory.py:100) and parsed its PLY header (inventory.py:112). inventory.json records its sha256, vertex and face counts and exporter comment. No geometry was used.\",\n      \"fix\": \"Correct the wording. Do not re-inventory, because the inventory sha seeds the DEV-CHECK draw.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F7\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor (report-only BROAD)\",\n      \"area\": \"BROAD gold ceilings not flagged\",\n      \"finding\": \"Two A1 BROAD golds cannot be fully matched by a recipe-guided engine, and neither is flagged. pc_d45186653eed (11979003 STL) has 9 AI-gold lines against a 7-bend recipe; this is the known window-merge convention conflict, and the owner's convention says one line. pc_38091ac91d9d (28870000 FULL) has 2 lines against a 1-bend recipe; the second bend is an E1 UNSUPPORTED rolled-feature joint. Both cap their family's F1 below 0.80 whatever the engine does.\",\n      \"fix\": \"Add flags such as GOLD_CONVENTION_CONFLICT or RECIPE_EXCLUDED_FEATURE, or make those cases recall-only, before freezing. Otherwise record the ceiling next to the 0.80 aim.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F8\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"area\": \"Legacy arm conditions\",\n      \"finding\": \"The code is unchanged, but the arm runs with a 4 GiB RSS cap. The line contract allows 12 GiB (SHERMAN_LINE_RSS_LIMIT_MB) and the broad baseline used 9 GiB. One DEV-CHECK legacy run was killed and counts as a legacy failure, which makes 'coverage >= legacy' and 'no worse than legacy' easier there. The config/NONE choice matches survey contract \u00a76 and is acceptable: on A1 its failures are identical to the API-config runtime lane (8/8). The worker also reads output/unary_models/latest.json when that file exists; no A1 report shows it was used (0/15 have structured_context), but the condition is not pinned.\",\n      \"fix\": \"Re-run that case with up to 12 GiB (under the 16 GiB rule), or score it NOT_EVALUABLE for the legacy comparisons. Pin or record the unary-model condition.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"F9\",\n      \"severity\": \"nit\",\n      \"area\": \"Reviewer-blind placement and wording\",\n      \"finding\": \"g3_truth_material/_reviewer_blind/ sits inside the reviewer-facing tree and is A1-readable. It holds an automated placement formed-set per case: not truth, but an anchoring risk. The relabel dual report reads the DEV-CHECK cases' relabel files during A1 scoring, though nothing from them reaches the output. 'No engine run' before the superseded draws should read 'no E3 run', since the legacy arm had already run in pass 1.\",\n      \"fix\": \"Move _reviewer_blind into the work directory or a SEALED-named location. Fix the wording.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"verified_ok\": [\n    \"6a: 11/11 Gold11 cases (71 lines) and 2 human non-Gold11 cases recovered, 0 excluded. gold_transforms.json was written at 19:14:37Z, before cases, lanes and dry-run scoring (19:23Z or later); scored_before_this_list=false. Scan, label and display-cloud sha256 re-verified on all A1 rows. Identity residual recomputed at 0.000000 mm on 4 cases, one of them an STL. The C05/C06 labels are scan_raw bound to the scan by sha256, so their residual is 0 by declaration.\",\n    \"4d: DEV 24/26, strict V10 20/26, native 18/26. Failures stay in the denominators (37126000 NO_RECIPE, 47479000 BLOCKED). The only exclusions are 2 UNSUPPORTED-rule rolled-feature candidates (28870000 and Default.stp, the same part). No SKU, family or filename logic in compile/. The policy sha 2ea6e87a matches ENGINE_COMPILE.md and every row. All 60 source-tree variant cells are identical to pass 1. I recompiled 3 public recipes myself; their compiled_part_sha256 is byte-identical. Recipes are opaque (DEV-<hex>, cad_<sha12>.step), FINAL, with both sides REQUIRED.\",\n    \"DEV-CHECK: 7/22 families (0.318), including 2 staged and 2 Gold11 families; the E2E part is ineligible. Zero overlap with every A1 id list, gold file, reference lane, legacy directory, G3 directory and reviewer-blind file. The V4 draw re-derives exactly from its recorded seed inputs and the frozen inventory sha. Superseded V2 and V3 are recorded in the sealed file only.\",\n    \"Legacy: backend/**, domains/bend/** and scripts/** are byte-identical to the G5 baseline manifest (2026-10-16T22:45Z). domains/reporting is unchanged. Fingerprint 3f445d5c reproduces. A1: 23 runs (15 OK, 8 WORKER_ERROR), the same failure set as the broad runtime lane.\",\n    \"Ledger: entry hash, entry_id, anchor, 42 file items, recipe list sha, scanner card, 5 threshold documents, 6 seed sets, 4 code fingerprints and all 6 sealed-item hashes reproduce under an independent canonicaliser. Plan \u00a75 and \u00a710 copy is byte-identical. `prefreeze verify` reports ok. The ledger contains no SEALED path.\",\n    \"G3 material: no E3, legacy or stage-key input in the code path. engine_output_used=false for all 27 A1 cases. A spot-check of the overlay and section images shows only opaque references and recipe labels. No E3 output exists yet.\",\n    \"No EHO4, HOLDOUT, N001-N016, codex-fetch or FRESH-SEALED identifier appears in any freeze, legacy or G3 output. All 60 BROAD rows are CONSUMED in BENCHMARK_V2. BROAD exclusions are consistent: 36 qualify, 21 have no STEP, 2 do not compile, 1 is OBJ.\"\n  ],\n  \"checks\": [\n    {\"cmd\": \"pytest (the exact named command) on 9 test_prod_engine_freeze_*.py files + test_prod_engine_eval_freeze.py + test_prod_engine_eval_runner.py, under the shared lock\", \"passed\": true, \"note\": \"81 passed in 82.2 s; lock released; no __pycache__ written\"},\n    {\"cmd\": \"prefreeze verify (without sealed files)\", \"passed\": true, \"note\": \"chain ok, anchor matches, no mismatches, no drift, fingerprints unchanged\"},\n    {\"cmd\": \"scratchpad/review_e4b/verify_ledger.py (independent re-hash)\", \"passed\": true, \"note\": \"every ledger item reproduces, sealed items as booleans only\"},\n    {\"cmd\": \"scratchpad/review_e4b/check_devcheck.py (counts only)\", \"passed\": false, \"note\": \"the lists are disjoint, but gold_transforms.json and inventory.json carry sealed identifiers and the work directory holds unsealed DEV-CHECK gold (F1, F3)\"},\n    {\"cmd\": \"scratchpad/review_e4b/recheck_gold.py, 4 residuals recomputed, under the lock\", \"passed\": true, \"note\": \"0.000000 mm\"},\n    {\"cmd\": \"E1 CLI recompile of DEV-1F88D309A7, DEV-81C428A0A5, DEV-BDE878D2AF, under the lock\", \"passed\": true, \"note\": \"compiled_part_sha256 identical\"},\n    {\"cmd\": \"G5 manifest comparison for backend, domains/bend and scripts\", \"passed\": true, \"note\": \"0 changed, 0 missing; only scripts/production files are new (excluded from the manifest) plus the allowlisted run_production_line_checks.sh\"}\n  ],\n  \"next_steps_before_A1\": [\n    \"E4b fix pass for F1, F2, F3 and F6, then `prefreeze ledger --replace-before-a1` and `verify`; R1 records the new anchor\",\n    \"Owner/orchestrator decision on F4, recorded in the ledger\",\n    \"G3 reviewers fill and freeze the truth table and record it in the ledger before A1's first run-physical (F5)\",\n    \"Timing: no new-engine (A1) numbers exist yet, and A1 should start only after the items above. The Jev-assisted A/B was not part of this review.\"\n  ],\n  \"files\": [\n    \"/Users/idantal/ShermanQC/FullProject/domains/production/engine/eval/freeze/prefreeze.py\",\n    \"/Users/idantal/ShermanQC/FullProject/domains/production/engine/eval/freeze/physical.py\",\n    \"/Users/idantal/ShermanQC/FullProject/domains/production/engine/eval/freeze/inventory.py\",\n    \"/Users/idantal/ShermanQC/FullProject/docs/production/runlog/freeze/README.md\",\n    \"/Users/idantal/ShermanQC/FullProject/docs/production/runlog/freeze/gold_transforms.json\",\n    \"/Users/idantal/ShermanQC/FullProject/docs/production/runlog/freeze/inventory.json\",\n    \"/Users/idantal/ShermanQC/FullProject/docs/production/runlog/g3_truth_material/_reviewer_blind\",\n    \"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-idantal/db065cf7-f766-4885-b217-ed8d7edd7ade/scratchpad/e4b_work\",\n    \"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-idantal/db065cf7-f766-4885-b217-ed8d7edd7ade/scratchpad/review_e4b/verify_ledger.py\",\n    \"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-idantal/db065cf7-f766-4885-b217-ed8d7edd7ade/scratchpad/review_e4b/check_devcheck.py\",\n    \"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-idantal/db065cf7-f766-4885-b217-ed8d7edd7ade/scratchpad/review_e4b/recheck_gold.py\"\n  ]\n}\n```"